1
00:00:00,318 --> 00:00:07,450
Want to apply for a PAN card online? Let's learn the full process step by step on Protean's official website.

2
00:00:07,832 --> 00:00:12,011
In this video I'll cover filling the form, documents, fees and checking the status.

3
00:00:12,965 --> 00:00:16,970
First, open this official Protean website in your browser.

4
00:00:17,352 --> 00:00:22,733
It clearly says that from 1 April 2026, new forms apply for a new PAN.

5
00:00:23,115 --> 00:00:27,551
For Indian citizens, Form No. 93 is now used.

6
00:00:27,933 --> 00:00:31,515
Fill this form only if you have never applied for a PAN before.

7
00:00:32,696 --> 00:00:35,475
Before applying, check the list of documents.

8
00:00:35,857 --> 00:00:39,462
You need three kinds of proof: Identity, Address and Date of Birth.

9
00:00:39,844 --> 00:00:43,240
Look carefully: Aadhaar works for Identity and Address.

10
00:00:43,622 --> 00:00:45,775
But for Date of Birth, it says No.

11
00:00:46,157 --> 00:00:51,512
So for Date of Birth, keep a document like a passport, driving licence or voter ID.

12
00:00:51,894 --> 00:00:55,138
A Class 10 marksheet also works as Date of Birth proof.

13
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,353
Now let's look at the fees.

14
00:00:57,735 --> 00:01:03,937
If you send documents by post (physical mode), the PAN card fee is ₹107.

15
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:08,917
In paperless mode (e-KYC & e-Sign), the fee is ₹101.

16
00:01:09,299 --> 00:01:12,625
If you only need an e-PAN, it costs ₹72 in physical mode.

17
00:01:13,006 --> 00:01:15,495
And in paperless mode, this fee is ₹66.

18
00:01:15,876 --> 00:01:19,667
Choosing e-Sign adds a separate charge of ₹5.90.

19
00:01:20,849 --> 00:01:25,746
Clicking the Apply link opens this Online PAN Application page.

20
00:01:26,128 --> 00:01:29,580
First, click the PAN Application Type dropdown.

21
00:01:29,962 --> 00:01:33,304
Then choose New PAN – Form No. 93 (Indian Citizen).

22
00:01:33,685 --> 00:01:37,626
Notice: once you choose Form 93, the Applicant Category dropdown disappears.

23
00:01:38,008 --> 00:01:41,032
Now fill in your name: First, Middle and Last Name.

24
00:01:42,281 --> 00:01:44,098
Do read the red note at the top.

25
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:48,328
If your Aadhaar name has initials, write the full name here.

26
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:53,089
The name as per Aadhaar is filled separately later, and that name is printed on the PAN card.

27
00:01:53,471 --> 00:01:56,355
Now enter Date of Birth, Email ID and Mobile Number.

28
00:01:58,107 --> 00:02:02,910
Use your own email and mobile, because the token number and updates come there.

29
00:02:03,292 --> 00:02:04,915
Now tick the consent box.

30
00:02:05,297 --> 00:02:07,605
Then fill the captcha below and click Submit.

31
00:02:07,987 --> 00:02:12,689
On submitting, a token number is generated, shown on screen and also sent by email.

32
00:02:13,071 --> 00:02:17,796
With this token number you can finish an incomplete form later via Resume Application.

33
00:02:18,796 --> 00:02:23,615
After the token, the next form opens. Let me explain these steps simply.

34
00:02:23,996 --> 00:02:25,812
There are four ways to submit the application.

35
00:02:26,194 --> 00:02:30,315
The easiest is e-KYC & e-Sign, where you don't have to send any papers.

36
00:02:30,697 --> 00:02:33,710
Then choose whether you want a physical PAN card or only an e-PAN.

37
00:02:34,092 --> 00:02:38,485
Next, fill personal details, name as per Aadhaar, address and contact details.

38
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:41,785
Then fill the AO Code, which depends on your city.

39
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:46,005
The AO Code is found on this AO Codes page of the website.

40
00:02:46,386 --> 00:02:48,610
Open the list here and pick the right code for your city.

41
00:02:49,610 --> 00:02:51,376
Now check the form and make the payment.

42
00:02:51,758 --> 00:02:56,777
In paperless mode you pay by credit card, debit card or net banking.

43
00:02:57,159 --> 00:03:00,561
After payment you get an acknowledgement with a 15-digit number.

44
00:03:00,943 --> 00:03:02,884
Its PDF also comes by email.

45
00:03:03,265 --> 00:03:12,524
In physical mode, send the signed acknowledgement, photos and documents to Protean's Pune office within 15 days.

46
00:03:12,905 --> 00:03:16,596
If everything is in order, the PAN card is normally dispatched in about two weeks.

47
00:03:17,778 --> 00:03:23,020
Now, checking status: you can track it three days after applying.

48
00:03:23,402 --> 00:03:26,255
Here, in Application Type, choose PAN – New / Change Request.

49
00:03:26,637 --> 00:03:29,944
Then enter the acknowledgement number and submit to see your status.

50
00:03:30,944 --> 00:03:35,259
So friends, this is how you apply for a new PAN card online on Protean's website.

51
00:03:35,641 --> 00:03:38,082
The full checklist is in the description.

52
00:03:38,464 --> 00:03:44,587
If you liked the video, please like and share, and subscribe to Learn Vexa. Thank you!

